# The tangent of a reciprocal sum in the positions and its derivative in a
# number that the charges depend on, q = q0 + lambda w, by two reciprocal
# sums with their forces (D379, #726), on the CPU.
# Inputs/tangent_pme.py writes the program and its oracle, the Ewald sum
# of the reciprocal space in NumPy in closed form (checked there against
# central differences). Each check prints the relative error against it,
# then 1 if within the tolerance that the script is given.
#
# REQUIRES: python-api
#
# Double precision, against the Ewald sum: the energy, the tangent, its
# derivative in lambda, dE/dlambda, the derivative of the tangent of a
# potential with a pair term besides (the same), and the tangent against
# -sum t . F of the same call.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/tangent_pme.py 2e-8 %t/double.mlir
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/double.mlir %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm --convert-ub-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
#
# Mixed precision, against the same sum.
#
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/tangent_pme.py 3e-5 %t/mixed.mlir
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/mixed.mlir %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_transforms \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-precision="mode=mixed" \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-algebra --md-exec-assign-storage --convert-md-exec-to-loops \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm --convert-ub-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
#
# Central differences along the tangent, by md-check-derivatives: the
# tangent against those of the energy, its derivative in lambda against
# those of derivative(lambda), at the step 1e-4 (the energy of the mesh
# carries a rounding of about 1e-10 of itself, which a smaller step
# amplifies). It aborts with a message on a value outside the tolerance.
#
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/tangent_pme.py 2e-8 %t/fd.mlir fd
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/fd.mlir --md-check-derivatives="step=1e-4 atol=1e-9 rtol=1e-6" \
# RUN:     %md_passes --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm --convert-ub-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FD

# CHECK-COUNT-6: {{^}}{{[0-9.e+-]+}}{{$}}{{[[:space:]]+}}1{{$}}
# FD-COUNT-5: {{^}}{{[0-9.e+-]+}}{{$}}{{[[:space:]]+}}1{{$}}
